c7-4e13"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\nThe completion-verifier LLM runs even when the ticket's own Acceptance Criteria block still contains unchecked '- [ ]' items — a deterministic fail-fast condition. Backtest over verifier-passed closes found unchecked boxes only in [operator-attested]-shaped items (whose done-evidence legitimately lives outside the snapshot); non-attested unchecked boxes did not occur, so a precheck that exempts the attested tag adds no false rejections. check-ac exists but only as a readiness scorer, absent from the close path.\n\n## Approach\nIn the close transition path (before the LLM verifier dispatch), parse the ticket description's '## Acceptance Criteria' section; if any '- [ ]' checkbox remains unchecked, fail the close deterministically with a teaching message (check the box after satisfying it, or edit the AC with justification) — same style as existing DET short-circuits. EXEMPTION: a '- [ ]' line whose text after the checkbox begins with the case-insensitive '[operator-attested]' tag is NOT a violation — reuse the exact matcher (det_operator_attested._OPERATOR_ATTESTED_TAG_RE, src/rebar/llm/plan_review/det_operator_attested.py:44) rather than a parallel regex, so the two surfaces cannot drift. Exempt classes that skip the verifier today (duplicate/not_a_bug/escalated via replacement-link precheck) are untouched: the precheck runs only where the verifier would run.\n\n## Scope\n- src/rebar/_commands/transition_close.py (precheck family, alongside _completion_precheck)\n- tests for the close path\n\n## Testing\nHappy: all boxes checked -> close proceeds to verifier. Unchecked box -> exit non-zero pre-LLM with the teaching message. Unchecked '- [ ] [operator-attested] ...' item -> precheck passes (exemption row, both lowercase and mixed-case tag). Non-completion classes (duplicate etc.) bypass unchanged. Description without checkbox syntax -> precheck passes (prose AC remains legal).\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Close on a ticket with any unchecked, non-[operator-attested] '- [ ]' AC item fails deterministically BEFORE any LLM call, with remediation guidance.\n- [ ] Unchecked items carrying the [operator-attested] tag (matched via det_operator_attested's shared regex) are exempt and do not block the close.\n- [ ] Prose-only AC (no checkboxes) and non-completion close classes are unaffected.\n- [ ] Backtest property preserved: historical verifier-passed closes (including attested-shaped ones) would all still pass.\n- [ ] Tests cover checked, unchecked, attested-exempt (case-insensitive), prose-only, and exempt-class paths.\n","env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/_commands/transition_close.py","reason":"close-time AC checkbox precheck"},{"path":"docs/plan-review-gate.md","reason":"document precheck"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","managed_refs":[["parent","2f4c-7e5c-e782-4e97"],["relates_to","4b54-6e28-45f7-42db"],["relates_to","5654-d048-43c7-4e13"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"2f4c-7e5c-e782-4e97","parent_status_uuid":"43f2e2fd-b1e4-4b20-a80f-b8cd9f1ae939","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":["gates"],"ticket_id":"433c-aa00-8ac1-49ae","ticket_type":"task","title":"AC-checkbox completeness precheck at close (deterministic, pre-LLM)","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["c4bba8cb-bb82-4ae2-879f-f0f33e244b54","48f627bf-e5d2-41af-8486-e26c3a0efcbe","a88deab2-ba74-44cb-9fa5-2d19e82a81d4","6c42c953-7c0c-46c3-85f6-69c7c23834d8","e2936e28-a751-4906-bc95-4a181be79a94","43f2e2fd-b1e4-4b20-a80f-b8cd9f1ae939","d3e913cf-05ba-47fc-88b4-24e105fa88f1","8c099b60-7b03-4a0b-9da7-128dbef6ea02"]},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1785719546809571479,"uuid":"1b9ee593-b7c6-42c2-9b20-55b20b793027"}